vely weak leadership skills.\n\nNow evaluate for long-distance pilot: need reliability, technical competence, calm under pressure, decision-making, teamwork/communication, professional development.\n\nCandidate C: high reliability, quick correct decisions, positive crew atmosphere (teamwork). Weakness: communication difficulty, egocentric, not willing to further education (professional development). Communication difficulty could be problematic for crew coordination. Egocentric may affect teamwork. But positive atmosphere suggests some teamwork.\n\nCandidate A: anticipates danger, sees complex connections, spatial vision, leadership. Weakness: not good at criticism, unorganized. Could affect teamwork and reliability. Unorganized may affect long flights.\n\nCandidate B: conscientious, handles stress, good weather assessment, computer skills. Weakness: grumpy, uncooperative. No teamwork strengths. Might be okay technically but poor crew interaction.\n\nCandidate D: problem solving, concentration, responsibility, handles unexpected events. Weakness: arrogant, weak leadership. Arrogance may affect crew cooperation. Weak leadership may be issue.\n\nWe need to weigh. Reliability: C is 100% reliable. A unknown reliability. B conscientious but uncooperative. D takes responsibility seriously.\n\nTechnical competence: A (spatial vision, anticipate dangerous situations) good. B (weather assessment, computer). C (quick decisions) maybe. D (problem solving, concentration).\n\nCalmness under pressure: B handles stress well. D responds to unexpected events adequately. A anticipates dangerous situations (maybe proactive). C makes quick correct decisions.\n\nTeamwork/communication: C creates positive atmosphere but difficulty communicating ideas. A has leadership qualities but not good at criticism. B uncooperative, grumpy. D arrogant, weak leadership.\n\nProfessional development: C not willing to further education (negative). A unorganized (maybe not development). B conscientious (maybe good). D unknown.\n\nOverall, candidate C seems strong on reliability and crew atmosphere, but communication difficulty and lack of willingness to develop may be concerning for long flights where continuous learning is needed. Candidate B strong on stress handling and technical weather, but poor teamwork. Candidate D strong technical and decision under pressure, but arrogance and weak leadership may hinder crew. Candidate A strong anticipation and leadership, but unorganized and poor at criticism.\n\nWhich is best? Probably candidate C due to reliability and positive crew atmosphere, despite communication difficulty. But we need to consider that communication difficulty could be mitigated? Not sure. The tradeoff: C's egocentric and lack of further education may be risk for long-term suitability. D's arrogance may be severe for crew. B's uncooperative is also severe. A's unorganized may affect safety.\n\nThus provisional preference: Candidate C.\n\nWe should note uncertainty: communication difficulty and lack of willingness to further education are concerns. If we had more info on B's teamwork or D's leadership, could shift.\n\nNow produce output."}
